     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;m sorry, I don&#39;t have the time to go into specifics and solve this problem. To reiterate: every single input must have a different, unique inputId parameter.  In the first code you provided, all the inputs had the id &quot;a&quot;, which means you would not be able to retrieve the values of all the different inputs.  In the code you just provided, the inputId is given by `B[i]`, but the B vector only has 3 elements, so if you try to change the num input to any number larger than 3, you should get an error.</div>"
